+---
+title: Stop a flow when an action fails
+date: 2026-11-20
+area: business-ops
+tags: [flow, message-queue, retry]
+---
+
+## Context
+
+[Retry failed flow actions](./_superseded/2025-04-08-retry-failed-flow-actions.md)
+retries a failed action and then continues with the next one. Continuing after
+the third failure ran later actions, such as the shipping mail, on orders whose
+payment action had failed.
+
+## Decision
+
+A flow action that throws is not retried. The error is logged and the flow
+stops, so later actions never run on a half-processed order. Merchants replay
+the flow from the flow log in the Administration.
+
+## Consequences
+
+* Flow actions must stay idempotent, because the message queue can still
+  deliver the same message twice.
+* A short outage of a mail server or webhook target stops the flow until a
+  merchant replays it.
